Error [jet.MarkedFunctionValue]: `consume` can't be used as a function value because its parameter `value` is `^`
  --> tests/ui/ownership/named_write_and_move_functions_cannot_erase_access_as_function_values_2.jet:3:24
    |
  3 | fn run() { callback :: consume }
    |                        ^^^^^^^
 Why: A function type gives each parameter plain read access, so a value of `consume` would drop the `^` its callers must write
 Fix: Call `consume` directly with the `^` mark, or pass a lambda that makes that call
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0227
